From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K11MCH1 <81425424+K11MCH1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:37:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Emit pending flushes where a suspended render pass chain
 starts

Turnip defers a dynamic render pass, and the cache flushes pending
before it, to tu_cmd_render(). When a suspend/resume chain is still
suspended at vkEndCommandBuffer(), tu_insert_dynamic_cmdbufs() renders
the chain at submit time from a new internal command buffer whose cache
state has no flush bits. The command buffer the chain started in ends
inside the suspended pass, so tu_EndCommandBuffer() only flushes the
render pass cache, and the flushes and waits of barriers recorded just
before the chain are never emitted.

On A8XX, where the CP no longer waits implicitly before reading indirect
arguments, a COMPUTE_SHADER -> DRAW_INDIRECT barrier then loses its
CP_WAIT_FOR_ME and wait-for-idle, and indirect draws in the chain read
their arguments before the compute shader has written them.
vkd3d-proton records render passes this way (suspended in one command
buffer, drawn in the next, stored in a third), so Unreal Engine 5
Nanite and virtual shadow map draws read stale arguments: the near
ground is black or over-shadowed in Mortal Shell 2. TU_DEBUG=flushall
hides it.

Emit the pending flushes in the command buffer where the chain starts.
No barrier can be recorded inside the chain, so nothing else is pending
when it is rendered. A test that writes the arguments from a long
compute dispatch and draws them in a chain split across two command
buffers of one submission drew nothing 30 times out of 30 on an Adreno
840 before this change and passes with it, in sysmem and GMEM.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index b347a33..fc854d2 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -7459,6 +7459,13 @@ tu_CmdBeginRendering(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
    cmd->state.suspending = suspending;
    cmd->state.resuming = resuming;
 
+   /* A chain still suspended at vkEndCommandBuffer() is rendered from a new
+    * command buffer by tu_insert_dynamic_cmdbufs(), which starts with no
+    * pending flushes, so emit the flushes of earlier barriers here.
+    */
+   if (suspending && !resuming)
+      tu_emit_cache_flush<CHIP>(cmd);
+
    if (!resuming && cmd->device->dbg_renderpass_stomp_cs) {
       tu_cs_emit_call(&cmd->cs, cmd->device->dbg_renderpass_stomp_cs);
       cmd->state.dirty |= TU_CMD_DIRTY_COMPUTE_DESC_SETS;
